    "result": "Perfect! All tests are now passing. Here's what I fixed:\n\n## Summary of changes\n\n**1. Fixed toxicity metric calculation** (`src/eval/metrics.js`)\n   - The `toxicityMetric` function was incorrectly accepting a second parameter for `bannedTerms`. When `runEvaluations` called it with `(outputs, references)`, it was treating the references as banned terms, incorrectly flagging all outputs.\n   - Removed the `bannedTerms` parameter and changed it to always use the hardcoded `defaultBannedTerms`.\n\n**2. Added missing named exports** (`src/finetune/index.js`)\n   - The test was importing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only available in the default export.\n   - Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `DEFAULT_GOVERNANCE_TEMPLATE`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`.\n\nAll 28 tests now pass, and all public exports remain intact.",
